adr: 0230
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: dump-dispatch
why: Exactly one side of the comparison must be an enumeration constant. Accepting the first side that is one makes `nkVar = nkStr` -- two constants compared with each other, which dispatches on nothing -- into a tag test, and makes the *field* reported whichever side happened to be scanned second. The corpus case has no such comparison and would not notice; what it does notice is the field, because the reported `on kind` becomes `on ?` wherever the constant is written on the left.
--- old
        side := cond^.bnRhs;
        if EnumConstOf(side) <> nil then
          if konst = nil then konst := side else konst := nil;
--- new
        side := cond^.bnRhs;
        if EnumConstOf(side) <> nil then
          if konst = nil then konst := side;
